 "_comment": "Oświęcim, Poland: a closed loop of real public roads round the old town and over the River Soła twice, from OpenStreetMap. Driven clockwise from the start line on ul. Legionów (the west-bank straight, heading north-east): Rondo Płonki, right onto ul. Dąbrowskiego and over the Soła on Most Piastowski under the castle hill, through the old town on ul. Dąbrowskiego, right down ul. Plebańska (setts) into the Rynek Główny (setts), out of its south-west corner down ul. Jagiełły (one-way, south) to Rondo Górnego, right over the Soła again on Most Jagielloński, up to Rondo Solidarności and right back onto ul. Legionów. The loop stays in the town centre and on the riverside: it keeps at least 700 m from the Auschwitz-Birkenau memorial grounds, turns away from them at Rondo Solidarności (that road is barred), and no corner is named after them. Routed node by node (\"nodes\") because of the roundabouts. See tools/build_street_tracks.py for the keys.",
